    {
      "id": "O4xzhkf69leTIn6780knr",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 180.98159042808834,
      "y": 303.3578932528593,
      "width": 320.7958556659717,
      "height": 950,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aX",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 741586805,
      "version": 1139,
      "versionNonce": 139253141,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787487482726,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A -> 3\nB -> 3 \n\nWhat is the size of map means\nhow many labels\n-> there is 2\n\n-> but we can do any internal\none at a time by n gap\n\n-> How the fuck would i add this\nin the heap shit , what is the\nrole of heap here ? \n\n-> what does maxheap do ? it\nreturns minimum element in o(1)\ntime\n\n-> I think : we will add elements\nin heap and if heap is empty\nmeans peek returns null , it is an\nidle state , can this be valid ? \n\n-> What if we add [label ,\nnumber] in heap \n\n-> oh what if we use n , like run\nuntil n , if it is over n \nstop pulling out of the heap and\nrecharge until n get recharges\n\n-> We will use queue here, first\nof all push into the queue\n\n-> My question is : \n1. How to add in the quue ? \n2. What to add in the heap ? \n3. How to add in the heap ? ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A -> 3\nB -> 3 \n\nWhat is the size of map means how many labels\n-> there is 2\n\n-> but we can do any internal one at a time by n gap\n\n-> How the fuck would i add this in the heap shit , what is the role of heap here ? \n\n-> what does maxheap do ? it returns minimum element in o(1) time\n\n-> I think : we will add elements in heap and if heap is empty means peek returns null , it is an idle state , can this be valid ? \n\n-> What if we add [label , number] in heap \n\n-> oh what if we use n , like run until n , if it is over n \nstop pulling out of the heap and recharge until n get recharges\n\n-> We will use queue here, first of all push into the queue\n\n-> My question is : \n1. How to add in the quue ? \n2. What to add in the heap ? \n3. How to add in the heap ? ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
